# Cursor skills

Skills live in `.cursor/skills/<name>/` with a `SKILL.md` and optional `scripts/`.

## Naming

Use `get-` when the skill fetches information. Use `sync-` when it writes fetched data into the repo.

- One item: `get-<thing>` (e.g. `get-jira-ticket`, `get-jira-release`)
- A catalogue: `get-list-of-<things>` (e.g. `get-list-of-jira-releases`)
- Write-back: `sync-<thing>` (e.g. `sync-version-scenarios`)

Do not use `list-` as the verb. Keep list vs detail as separate skills.

```
# ❌ BAD
list-jira-releases
fetch-ticket
jira-release

# ✅ GOOD
get-list-of-jira-releases
get-jira-ticket
get-jira-release
sync-version-scenarios
```

## Public descriptions

This repo is public. `SKILL.md` (including `description` and examples) must stay generic.

- No site URLs, project keys, real ticket ids, or real release names
- Use placeholders: `KEY-123`, `PROJ`, `"1.0"`
- Point at env vars and script defaults instead of naming the instance

```
# ❌ BAD
Targets https://example.atlassian.net. Default project is ABC.
/get-jira-ticket ABC-99

# ✅ GOOD
Site comes from `ATLASSIAN_BASE_URL` if set, otherwise the script default.
/get-jira-ticket KEY-123
```

## Behaviour

- Put site/project defaults in scripts (or `ATLASSIAN_BASE_URL` / `JIRA_PROJECT`), not in skill text
- Write output under `.tmp/`
- If a script fails, stop; do not guess or scrape the UI
- Return full fetched contents; do not summarise
